// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0 tagged "button" (KEEP, capabilities set to
// ["digital_input","button"]) - vendor pins_arduino.h in
// espressif/arduino-esp32 (variants/wifiduino32/pins_arduino.h,
// added by PR #4218 "add board WiFiduino32") declares
// "static const uint8_t KEY_BUILTIN = 0;", identifying GPIO0 as the
// board's built-in button. This is the Blinker WiFiduino32 (ESP32,
// listed in PlatformIO's board index as "Blinker WiFiduino32").
// GPIO0 is a standard ESP32 strapping/BOOT pin, pulled up and driven
// LOW when the onboard button is pressed - consistent with the
// chip-level pinNotes entry "Must be HIGH or floating on reboot".
// Checked this file's SDA/SCL/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK/TX/RX alias constants
// against GPIO0: none of them alias GPIO0 (SDA=5, SCL=16, SS=5,
// MOSI=23, MISO=19, SCK=18, TX=1, RX=3), so no bus-capability
// contamination applies to this pin and no alias lines needed to be
// removed.
